Blacksmith: You must be the one Chief told me about.
You: He sent me to collect some gear.
Blacksmith: That's right. I've prepared a basic set for you. Nothing fancy, but it'll give you some protection while you're training.
Blacksmith: Here you are. Make sure everything fits before you head out.
[signal arg="[signal arg="set_flag_training_gear_ready"]"]
You: These should help.
Litik: Hold on! Someone has just taken the time to prepare equipment for you. What's the proper way to thank them?
label thank_you_quiz
Litik: Which phrase means "Thank you very much"?
- Salamat!
	Litik: Close! That means "Thank you." It's polite, but there's a phrase that expresses even more gratitude.
	jump thank_you_quiz
- Dakal a salamat!
	Litik: Correct! "Dakal a salamat" means "Thank you very much."
	[signal arg="[signal arg="learn_dakal_a_salamat"]"]
	You: Dakal a salamat!
	Blacksmith: Ala pung nanu man!
	Blacksmith: Now, go back to Chief. He wants to see how well you can use that gear.
	[signal arg="[signal arg="set_flag_training_gear_received"]"]
	[end_timeline]
- Mayap a gatpanapun!
	Litik: That's "Good afternoon." It's a greeting, not a way to thank someone.
	jump thank_you_quiz
